{"id": "x0603", "pool": "know-open", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The process to become a Santero, or Santera, is a deep and meaningful journey rooted in tradition, faith, and personal commitment. It typically begins with a sincere desire to serve the Orishas, who are the deities central to Afro-Cuban Santeria. One usually starts by seeking out a dedicated spiritual leader known as a Babalawo or Olorisha, who can guide them through the initiation process. This often involves a series of rituals called k inchola, which help establish a spiritual connection between the individual and the Orishas. These ritual s may include offerings, prayers, meditation, and participation in ceremonies. Over time, the person gains deeper knowledge about the beliefs, practices, and cultural heritage associated with Sante ria. As they progress, they learn how to conduct ritual s, prepare sacred items like egun ti, and support others on their spiritual path. Becoming a fully recognized Santer o or Santera usually requires years of dedication, service, and continued growth under the guidance of their teacher.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 54, "carrier_ended": null}
