{"id": "x0699", "pool": "know-open", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The idea of return to nature was popularized by the German philosopher Friedrich Na gel, who believed that humans should seek a deeper connection with nature.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0707", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is A, wind energy. Wind energy is generated by air convection currents. These current s are created when warm air rises and cool air sink s, causing movement in the atmosphere. Wind turbines harness this natural movement to produce electricity.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0715", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 12, "onset_chunk": 11, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Plants can use underground water. That's the right answer. When there's a drought, plants have an advantage because they' re rooted in the ground and can tap into that hidden water supply beneath the surface. Animals can't do that, so they're more vulnerable when it gets really dry.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 14, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0723", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Acid rain is usually in the lower range of the pH scale, so it would most likely be option A, 4 to 6.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 7, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0731", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "I think the answer is D, wind.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 2, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0739", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 15, "onset_chunk": 14, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Two cities are located only 50 kilometers apart and yet the cities have different climates. Which of these factors is the most likely cause of this difference in climate? A, elevation, B, population, C, latitude, D, long itude.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0747", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 21, "onset_chunk": 21, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is a. an inference made from observations.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 3, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0755", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The characteristic of motion that could change without altering the velocity is C, the direction. Ve locity is a vector quantity, meaning it has both magnitude and direction. If you change the direction of an object' s motion while keeping its speed constant, its velocity changes because the direction component of the velocity vector shifts. So changing the direction is possible without changing the speed or overall velocity in terms of magnitude alone.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 25, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0763", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is D. Cold blooded.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0771", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is fertil ization, germination, and sexual reproduction. All of these occur in the life cycle of plants. F ertilization is when the sperm from a pollen grain un ites with an egg cell inside the flower. Ger min ation happens when a seed begins to grow into a new plant after conditions are right for it. And sexual reproduction involves the production of seeds or spores through the fusion of male and female gametes. Maturation, while important, is not necessarily a defining step that occurs in every single stage of all plant life cycle s as consistently as the other three processes. So, fer tilization, ger mination, and sexual reproduct ion are the key events found across all plant life cycles.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 37, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0779", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 11, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The similarity is that both carry energy. So sound waves and light waves are both forms of energy in motion, just traveling through different ways.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0787", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 22, "onset_chunk": 21, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is C. Water exists in all three states on Earth. When a forecast predict s a wintry mix of rain and snow, it means that water vapor in the air is changing into both liquid form as rain and solid form as snow. This shows that water can exist as vapor, liquid, and solid depending on temperature and conditions. So option C correctly describe s this phenomenon .", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 23, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0795", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 12, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The skin stabil izes temperature. That's correct.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
